.TH "git-drop" 1

.SH NAME
git-drop - safely delete a git branch with interactive confirmation and worktree safety checks

.SH SYNOPSIS
git drop <branch>

.SH DESCRIPTION
git\-drop \- delete a git branch safely.

Refuses to delete a branch that is checked out in another worktree. If the
branch is checked out in the current worktree, first checks out a fallback
branch, in order of preference:

.IP \(bu 2
The branch's upstream, if it tracks a local branch that is not checked out
elsewhere.
.IP \(bu 2
The default branch, if it is not checked out elsewhere.
.IP \(bu 2
A backup branch named <upstream>-kedgebk (or <default>-kedgebk without a
local upstream), created from that branch if needed.
.PP
Attempts to delete the branch with git branch -d. If that fails, shows the
latest commit and the commits unique to the branch, then prompts for
confirmation before using git branch -D.
